# Data, caches and figures are ignored everywhere. SCRIPTS AND DOCS ARE TRACKED.
#
# Reproduction/ was formerly ignored wholesale, via `Reproduction/**` on this line.
# The .m files already in git stayed tracked (an ignore rule does not untrack), but
# every NEW one was invisible to `git add` -- so a commit could pick up an edited
# caller while silently dropping the function it calls. The specific rules below
# already cover everything under Reproduction/ that should not be tracked: figures,
# _cache, _glmqc, and the *.pdf / *.mat / .DS_Store patterns further down.
Support/
Data/**
Manuscript draft/
Reproduction/figures/
Reproduction/**/_cache/
Reproduction/_glmqc/
dg_collect/
*.pdf
*.png
*.bmp
*.fig
*.edf
*.dat
*.m~
*.mat
.DS_Store
**/*.asv
**/*.html
__pycache__/
*.pyc
